zvolrescue reads the on-disk format of a ZFS pool by itself, without the
kernel's ZFS and without importing the pool, and writes the raw image of a
volume (zvol) out of it at any transaction group that still verifies: every
block through its checksum, mirror copies and RAIDZ or dRAID parity to heal
what one member cannot give, encrypted datasets with a key. It never writes
to the members, and it logs every run as evidence a third party can check.

With it: zvoltimeline (the pool's history from the transaction groups it
still carries), zvolcarve (volumes no uberblock points at any more, found in
raw vdev space), zvolfiles (files out of filesystem datasets) and zvolreport
(the evidence logs of the others as one signed, checkable report).
